# Public Invitation Pages

## Routing

- Public URL: `/w/[slug]` (e.g. `/w/rahul-weds-ananya`) — clean slugs, no numeric IDs
- Route: `src/app/w/[slug]/page.tsx`

## Server Rendering (Required)

WhatsApp/Instagram crawlers **do not run JavaScript**.

- Page must be a **React Server Component**
- Fetch the published snapshot from `published_invitations` on the server. Page rendering and metadata must share the same request-cached read. Never fall back to owner working content.
- Pass data to client `<TemplateRenderer />` as props

## Metadata

Use Next.js **`generateMetadata()`** for:

- `title`, `description`
- OpenGraph tags (`og:title`, `og:image`, `og:description`)
- WhatsApp preview image from invitation content when available

Inject metadata in `<head>` before client hydration.

## Hydration

Countdown and time-sensitive values: render placeholder on server; update in `useEffect` on client to prevent hydration mismatch.

## Performance

Guest opens link from WhatsApp on mobile data — prioritize fast LCP, minimal client JS, optimized hero image.

## Interactions (Royal)

- **Cinematic intro:** tap-to-open curtains; once per browser session; disabled in editor preview.
- **Scratch reveal:** hero wedding date; touch-friendly; skipped when `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **RSVP:** WhatsApp deep link or external URL only — no server-side guest storage on public pages.

## Access

- Published copies: public SELECT via RLS; no client writes.
- Working content in `invitations`: owner-only, even when status is published.
- Unpublish removes the public copy and preserves private edits/link history.
- Read [the persistence contract](../../docs/invitation-persistence.md); its migration is pending, with verification deferred to task 16.

## SEO

Dynamic metadata per couple; shareable premium preview — no spammy keyword stuffing.
